  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING CHANGES:\n- enforce deferred migration diagnostic boundaries\n  Require trimming and dynamic-code diagnostics when constructing deferred resolvers, and verify that packaged warnings explain the unsupported behavior. Validate package inputs and document the source-location contract used by consumer checks.\nNew Features:\n- support .NET 8 and .NET 9 without JSON upgrades\n  Add .NET 8 and .NET 9 assets so applications and plugin hosts can\n  use migration support with their framework-provided System.Text.Json.\n  Read resolved collection metadata through a .NET 8-only accessor;\n  .NET 9 and newer retain the public API path.\n  Preserve collection-routing behavior and cover resolver snapshot\n  retention and cyclic discovery on the applicable runtimes. Keep\n  compatibility guidance consistent and extend CI and packed-consumer\n  verification across all supported targets without changing other\n  packages or shared dependency versions.\n  Keep the retained framework assets buildable with newer SDKs after\n  their support end dates by disabling framework end-of-support checks\n  within this package and its isolated verification consumers.\n- allow legacy intermediates in chained migration edges\n  Allow migration contract implementations to reuse legacy types reachable from their source through self-targeted migration contracts. Preserve warnings for unrelated members and unreachable types, and bound recursive generic expansion to keep compilation responsive.\n  Add regression coverage for chained paths, direction, generic identity, cycles, and migration-method boundaries. Document the expanded STJM0010 exemption and its conservative generic-search limit.\n  Closes #263\nBug Fixes:\n- surface actionable trimming and NativeAOT warnings\n  Migration setup and registration now report standard trimming and NativeAOT diagnostics at consumer call sites, including configurations with generated JSON metadata. Messages explain the unsupported behavior and the deployment settings needed to avoid it.\n  Enable library analysis on both supported frameworks and verify the packed consumer contract without introducing a new registration API or changing service-provider activation.",
